{
  "_why": "Feature discovery is two surfaces over one ledger: a full-screen post-upgrade guide shown once per guide id while the control plane enables it, and an optional spotlight walkthrough. These vectors pin the observable rules so a refactor cannot silently regress them: the three KV row names and the localStorage mirror name, the ledger's accumulative-array shape, the guide seen-map's overwrite-whole shape, the guide's fail-closed due-ness (enable + guideId + unseen, with an on-screen exception so a refresh cannot unmount the page being read), the control-plane payload contract (a page list is accepted whole or not at all), and the tour markers and their start gates. All three KV rows must also stay out of SessionConfiguration staleness: acknowledging a hint happens while the user is looking at a new feature, so it may never rebuild a live session (pinned separately by tests/session-wire.test.ts).",
  "storage": {
    "ledgerKey": "onboarding.feature_seen",
    "guideSeenKey": "onboarding.guide_seen",
    "readingModeKey": "appearance.reading_mode",
    "mirrorKey": "klaus_onboarding_mirror",
    "uiOnlyKeys": [
      "onboarding.feature_seen",
      "onboarding.guide_seen",
      "appearance.reading_mode"
    ],
    "ledgerShape": [
      "workspace-files",
      "tour:workspace-files"
    ],
    "guideSeenShape": {
      "release-0.7": true
    },
    "mirrorShape": {
      "ledger": [
        "workspace-files"
      ]
    },
    "_mirrorHoldsLedgerOnly": "the guide decision also needs the control-plane config, which arrives asynchronously; a mirror that guessed it would show or hide a guide on the first frame from a value nobody validated"
  },
